<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Callann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1261</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Callann was fought in 1261 near Kilgarvan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-kerry">County Kerry</a>, Ireland, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finghin-mac-carthaigh">Fínghin Mac Carthaigh</a>, king of Desmond, defeated the Anglo-Norman FitzGeralds. John FitzThomas and his son Maurice were killed, and the victory checked Norman expansion into south-west Munster for generations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-callann.jpg" alt="Battle of Callann" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mike Searle · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Callan_Grave.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
